 "description": "The corporate HQ network as one contained twin: an MX85-shaped edge\nrouter (`hq-mx`) gatewaying the twelve real VLANs (1, 20, 32, 40, 48, 52,\n64, 192, 880, 1010 at the MX; 935, 953 at the 9K TOR pair), the lab and\nremote subnets the discovery saw routed through HQ, two ISP uplinks\n(WAN1 active to an any-IP sink standing in for Comcast and the internet,\nWAN2 present and idle), the network devices as VMs (MS120 core, access\nswitches, 3850, a 9K01/9K02 VRRP pair, the 8325h VSX pair -- 802.1Q\ntrunks, STP, a down port), and the ~133 hosts the axquery discovery cast\nobserved above the deploy gate -- a real AD DS DC, 16 joined Windows\nworkstations, bind9/nginx/Samba servers, and Linux endpoints -- driven by\nthe cast's own personas.\n",
